ROYA v1 Knowledge Base
This document serves as the central repository for summarized technical specifications of the ROYA v1 system.

1. Core Engines & Components
ROYA_Shared_Components_v1
Purpose: Foundational schemas and interfaces for the entire ROYA system.
Key Contracts:
Lead_v1: Canonical schema for lead data (UUID, Phone, Status, Metadata).
NormalizedMessage: Standard format for incoming/outgoing interactions.
Interfaces:
ChannelAdapter: Abstract communication (SMS, WhatsApp, Email).
CRMAdapter: Abstract lead management (HighLevel, Salesforce).
TraceEmitter / MetricsEmitter: Observability and analytics.
Design Philosophy: Stateless, contract-first, and stack-agnostic.
WF_WhatsApp_Decision_Engine_v1
Purpose: Specific implementation for WhatsApp channel.
Key Features: Message normalization, media handling (images/PTTs), session management, and rate limiting.
WF_SleepingBeauty_DBR_Engine_v1
Purpose: Reactivating dormant leads (DBR).
Process: CSV Ingestion → "Prince Charming Kiss" → Qualification Conversation → Appointment.
Metrics: 15%+ Response rate, 40%+ Qualification rate.
WF_SpeedToLead_Engine_v1
Purpose: Immediate response (<60s) to fresh leads.
Process: Webhook Trigger → Normalization → Initial Acknowledgment → Routing.
NFR: Sustained throughput of 500 leads/hour.
WF_OutOfHours_Engine_v1
Purpose: Managing leads received outside business hours.
Process: Time Detection → Automated Nurturing → Sales Handoff (during work hours).
WF_DocumentCollection_Engine_v1
Purpose: Automated document requests and validation.
Key Features: Milestone triggers, smart follow-ups (backoff), structural validation, payment milestone triggers.
Target: Completion in ≤ 48 hours.
2. Cross-Cutting Systems
ROYA_Compliance_Guardrails_v1
Purpose: Legal enforcement (TCPA, GDPR) across all engines.
Controls: Explicit consent, opt-out management, frequency limits, PII masking in logs.
ROYA_Analytics_Metrics_v1
Purpose: Framework for measurement and ROI attribution.
Reporting: Response/Qualification/Appointment rates, revenue attribution, cost per lead.
Observability: Prometheus/Datadog ready metrics emission.
3. Infrastructure & Deployment
Environment Variable Standardization
ROYA v1 uses a unified environment variable pattern across all engines to ensure security and portability.

Pattern: $env.VARIABLE_NAME
Critical Variables: WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID, META_LONG_LIVED_TOKEN, HUBSPOT_APP_TOKEN.
Docker Architecture
The system is optimized for containerized deployment via Docker Compose.

Benefits: Environment isolation, unified credential injection, and high availability.
Components: n8n container + Persistent Volumes (n8n_data).
Configuration: 
docker-compose.yml